00:33:44.110 --> 00:33:44.770
His cafe disco.
你会看到凯文在那里笨手笨脚地做他的浓缩咖啡。

800
00:33:45.210 --> 00:33:50.030
And you'll see that Kevin is there very messily making his espresso.
你会看到凯文在那里笨手笨脚地做他的浓缩咖啡。

801
00:33:50.250 --> 00:33:52.370
And it's because he's waiting for Lynn.
那是因为他在等琳恩。

802
00:33:52.810 --> 00:33:57.510
Had you seen all of that deleted runner, you would know he's hoping Lynn will show up.
如果你看了所有删减片段，就会知道他在期待琳恩出现。

803
00:33:57.770 --> 00:34:00.630
In fact, in the shooting draft, the scene is more extended.
事实上，在拍摄剧本里，这场戏更长一些。

804
00:34:00.870 --> 00:34:03.070
And Kevin tells Michael he's waiting for Lynn.
凯文告诉迈克尔他在等琳恩。

805
00:34:03.230 --> 00:34:03.690
Wow.
哇。

806
00:34:04.150 --> 00:34:05.050
Before Angela enters.
在安吉拉进来之前。

807
00:34:05.830 --> 00:34:09.490
And this scene, when I enter, I could barely get through, Jenna.
还有这场戏，我进来的时候，珍娜，我简直快演不下去了。

808
00:34:09.850 --> 00:34:14.010
I think you can tell I'm breaking if you watch it because whenever Steve as Michael
我想如果你仔细看的话，能看出我快憋不住笑了，因为每当史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔

809
00:34:14.010 --> 00:34:19.250
offers Kevin the fake cookie in his hand, I literally, I start smiling when I talk because
把手里那块假饼干递给凯文时，我真的，我说话的时候就开始笑了，因为

810
00:34:19.250 --> 00:34:21.330
I'm having such a hard time not laughing.
我实在太难忍住不笑了。

811
00:34:21.550 --> 00:34:23.350
It's so absurd and wonderful.
这太荒谬也太精彩了。

812
00:34:23.670 --> 00:34:27.370
And a lot of that is Brian Baumgartner's performance.
这很大程度上归功于布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳的表演。

813
00:34:27.590 --> 00:34:27.910
Yes.
没错。

814
00:34:28.030 --> 00:34:33.030
His, like, immediate belief that there's a cookie in a hand that clearly didn't have
他那种，怎么说呢，立刻就相信了手里有饼干，明明一秒钟前

815
00:34:33.030 --> 00:34:34.170
a cookie one second ago.
手里根本没有饼干。

816
00:34:34.170 --> 00:34:34.690
Yes.
是的。

817
00:34:35.050 --> 00:34:38.610
Well, the three of us improvised the whole last couplet of dialogue.
其实，最后那两句对话是我们三个人即兴发挥的。

818
00:34:38.810 --> 00:34:39.510
No way.
不会吧。

819
00:34:39.730 --> 00:34:39.970
Yes.
真的。

820
00:34:40.130 --> 00:34:42.210
So in the script, I mean, the script was phenomenal.
剧本里，我是说，剧本本身已经非常棒了。

821
00:34:42.470 --> 00:34:47.750
But as we started doing it, Steve, as Michael, just kept messing with Kevin.
但当我们开始拍的时候，史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔一直在逗凯文。

822
00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:51.110
He kept showing him the cookie, but then pulling it a little out of reach.
他一直给凯文看饼干，但又稍微往回缩一点。

823
00:34:51.250 --> 00:34:53.110
So Kevin had to walk further into the room.
所以凯文不得不往房间里多走几步。

824
00:34:53.450 --> 00:34:55.790
And that was just stuff we were making up on the day.
那些都是我们当天临时想出来的。

825
00:34:55.990 --> 00:34:59.710
Well, in the script, it was just a little cleaner of an ending, right?
剧本里的结尾其实更简洁一点，对吧？

826
00:34:59.710 --> 00:35:00.530
It was a little simpler.
更简单一些。

827
00:35:00.730 --> 00:35:02.430
It was like, Michael said, Kevin, stay.
大概是迈克尔说：凯文，留下。

828
00:35:02.610 --> 00:35:03.630
Angela said, Kevin, come.
安吉拉说：凯文，过来。

829
00:35:03.890 --> 00:35:05.290
And then Michael's like, Kevin, cookie.
然后迈克尔说：凯文，饼干。

830
00:35:05.470 --> 00:35:06.370
And then Kevin's like, what?
接着凯文说：什么？

831
00:35:06.450 --> 00:35:06.970
There's a cookie?
有饼干吗？

832
00:35:07.490 --> 00:35:08.850
And then I drag him away.
然后我就把他拉走了。

833
00:35:09.190 --> 00:35:11.690
We just had so much fun with this fake cookie.
我们玩这块假饼干玩得太开心了。

834
00:35:11.890 --> 00:35:16.630
We just improvised this little couplet at the end where Kevin's like, wait, is there a cookie?
我们即兴加了最后那两句，凯文说：等等，有饼干吗？

835
00:35:16.750 --> 00:35:17.450
And Michael's like, mm-hmm.
迈克尔说：嗯哼。

836
00:35:17.650 --> 00:35:20.770
And I'm like, no, for goodness sakes, Kevin, there's no cookie.
我说：不，天哪，凯文，根本没有饼干。

837
00:35:20.850 --> 00:35:21.430
There's no cookie.
没有饼干。

838
00:35:21.550 --> 00:35:21.910
Come on.
快走吧。

839
00:35:21.910 --> 00:35:23.010
And I kind of like show him.
我还给凯文看了看。

840
00:35:23.110 --> 00:35:24.710
I'm trying to pry Michael's hand.
我试图掰开迈克尔的手。

841
00:35:24.850 --> 00:35:24.990
Yes, yes.
对，没错。

842
00:35:25.130 --> 00:35:26.770
And Kevin's like, I wanted a cookie.
凯文说：我还想要饼干呢。

843
00:35:26.770 --> 00:35:29.350
And then I look back at Michael, and I'm like, completely unacceptable.
然后我回头看着迈克尔，说：这简直不可理喻。

844
00:35:29.710 --> 00:35:30.890
It was so fun.
太好玩了。

845
00:35:31.010 --> 00:35:31.890
We had a blaSt.
我们玩得超开心。

846
00:35:32.470 --> 00:35:36.350
And somewhere out there, there's just footage of me laughing every time.
在某个地方，肯定存着我每次都笑场的花絮。

847
00:35:36.690 --> 00:35:39.490
Kevin looks at Michael's hand and is like, what is there a cookie?
凯文看着迈克尔的手说：什么，有饼干吗？

848
00:35:39.750 --> 00:35:40.750
It's so good.
太棒了。

849
00:35:41.290 --> 00:35:42.810
Well, now Michael is alone.
好了，现在迈克尔一个人待着了。

850
00:35:43.290 --> 00:35:45.170
He really wants people to come.
他真的很希望有人能来。

851
00:35:45.290 --> 00:35:49.630
So he is going to blast music through the vent.
所以他打算通过通风口播放音乐。

852
00:35:49.870 --> 00:35:50.270
Yes.
没错。

853
00:35:50.270 --> 00:35:52.790
And people up in the bullpen can hear it.
楼上办公区的人都能听见。

854
00:35:52.890 --> 00:35:56.530
And everyone kind of starts, you know, moving and grooving a little bit.
大家都有点跟着节奏动起来了。

855
00:35:56.750 --> 00:35:59.950
So much so that Phyllis decides she's going to go.
菲利斯甚至决定她也要去。

856
00:36:00.130 --> 00:36:01.470
Yeah, she says, to heck with it.
是啊，她说管他呢。

857
00:36:01.610 --> 00:36:08.330
But first, she's going to stop by Vance Refrigeration to invite Bob, where she runs into Bob's younger,
但她先去了一趟万斯制冷公司想邀请鲍勃，结果在那儿碰到了鲍勃年轻的、

858
00:36:09.030 --> 00:36:10.970
yet sort of lookalike secretary.
长得还有点像她的秘书。

859
00:36:11.330 --> 00:36:13.850
This is how this character was described in the script.
剧本里就是这么描述这个角色的。

860
00:36:14.130 --> 00:36:19.810
As Phyllis walks in, Bob's busty secretary, Jessica, is coming out of Bob's office
菲利斯走进去时，鲍勃那胸部丰满的秘书杰西卡正从鲍勃办公室出来，

861
00:36:19.810 --> 00:36:21.250
and closing the door behind her.
并随手关上了门。

862
00:36:21.470 --> 00:36:23.330
She wears a low-cut top.
她穿着一件低胸上衣。

863
00:36:23.830 --> 00:36:25.410
Phyllis looks her up and down.
菲利斯上下打量了她一番。

864
00:36:25.770 --> 00:36:26.690
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

865
00:36:26.690 --> 00:36:32.590
So it doesn't mention that she's meant to sort of be this younger version of Phyllis.
剧本里没提她应该是菲利斯的年轻版。

866
00:36:32.730 --> 00:36:35.250
Because they dressed her just like Phyllis dresses.
因为剧组给她穿的衣服跟菲利斯平时的穿搭一模一样。

867
00:36:35.570 --> 00:36:35.620
I know.
我知道。

868
00:36:35.710 --> 00:36:36.090
I know.
我知道。

869
00:36:36.090 --> 00:36:39.990
And I felt like even, like, their little noses were similar and everything.
我觉得甚至连她们的小鼻子什么的都很像。

870
00:36:40.230 --> 00:36:41.250
Their hairstyles.
还有发型。

871
00:36:41.310 --> 00:36:41.690
Yes.
没错。

872
00:36:41.930 --> 00:36:45.830
She's clearly like what Phyllis would think Bob would want in a younger woman.
她显然就是菲利斯认为鲍勃会喜欢的年轻女性的样子。

873
00:36:45.990 --> 00:36:46.410
Yes.
没错。

874
00:36:46.770 --> 00:36:49.350
Which I thought was such a great casting choice.
我觉得这个选角真是太棒了。

875
00:36:49.630 --> 00:36:53.190
The woman who played Jessica was Alyssa Preston.
饰演杰西卡的演员是艾丽莎·普雷斯顿。

876
00:36:53.770 --> 00:36:59.770
And according to her IMDb, this job was her first television credit.
根据她的IMDb资料，这份工作是她第一个电视作品。

877
00:37:00.010 --> 00:37:01.410
Oh, she did so great.
噢，她演得太好了。

878
00:37:01.730 --> 00:37:03.470
Do you remember your first television job?
你还记得你的第一份电视工作吗？

879
00:37:03.470 --> 00:37:04.630
Oh, God, I do.
天哪，我记得。

880
00:37:05.150 --> 00:37:05.730
What was it?
是什么？

881
00:37:05.730 --> 00:37:06.570
I think I was horrible.
我觉得我当时演得糟透了。

882
00:37:06.790 --> 00:37:07.530
What was it?
是什么？

883
00:37:07.670 --> 00:37:11.850
Oh, my very first line on a television show was a TV show called Step by Step.
噢，我在电视节目里的第一句台词是在一部叫《一步一步来》的剧里。

884
00:37:12.090 --> 00:37:14.890
The big stars were Suzanne Somers and Patrick Duffy.
当时的大明星是苏珊·萨默斯和帕特里克·达菲。

885
00:37:15.130 --> 00:37:16.790
Was it a three-camera show?
那是三机位拍摄的剧吗？

886
00:37:16.970 --> 00:37:18.430
It was a multi-camera show.
那是多机位拍摄的剧。

887
00:37:18.570 --> 00:37:21.810
In the episode, they think their daughter has run off to elope.
在那一集里，他们以为自己的女儿私奔去结婚了。

888
00:37:22.010 --> 00:37:27.730
And I was cast because I was the same height and same hair color as the young girl playing
我被选中是因为我的身高和发色跟那个饰演他们女儿的女孩一样，

889
00:37:27.730 --> 00:37:28.270
their daughter.
所以选了我。

890
00:37:29.270 --> 00:37:35.370
And they burst into this wedding chapel, like in Vegas or somewhere.
他们冲进了一座婚礼教堂，好像是在拉斯维加斯还是什么地方。

891
00:37:35.610 --> 00:37:38.890
They burst in, and I'm up there saying my vows.
他们冲了进来，而我正站在那儿宣读誓词。

892
00:37:39.110 --> 00:37:42.290
So Suzanne Somers whips me around at the altar.
然后苏珊·萨默斯在祭坛前猛地把我转过来。

893
00:37:42.490 --> 00:37:44.510
And she goes, you're not Dana.
她说，你不是达娜。

894
00:37:44.730 --> 00:37:46.890
And I say, no, I'm Simone.
我说，不，我是西蒙娜。

895
00:37:47.010 --> 00:37:50.330
And thanks for ruining the best day of my life.
还有，谢谢你毁了我一生中最美好的一天。

896
00:37:50.970 --> 00:37:51.530
Wow.
哇。

897
00:37:51.530 --> 00:37:51.670
Wow.
哇。

898
00:37:53.450 --> 00:37:55.110
It's like crazy that I remember that.
真疯狂，我居然还记得这些。

899
00:37:55.470 --> 00:37:56.930
And I auditioned for it.
我当时还去试镜了。

900
00:37:57.190 --> 00:38:00.270
And it wasn't for like two months later that I shot it.
而且过了大概两个月我才去拍摄的。

901
00:38:00.650 --> 00:38:04.870
And I said to the director that day, I said, how do you want me to do it?
那天我对导演说，我说，你希望我怎么演？

902
00:38:05.070 --> 00:38:06.630
And he said, just like you did in the audition.
他说，就照你试镜时那样演。

903
00:38:06.870 --> 00:38:08.730
I couldn't remember how I did it in the audition.
但我根本不记得我试镜时是怎么演的了。

904
00:38:08.950 --> 00:38:09.130
Oh, no.
噢，不。

905
00:38:09.390 --> 00:38:12.290
And then when I did it, they were like, can you tone it down?
后来我演的时候，他们就说，能不能收敛一点？

906
00:38:12.490 --> 00:38:17.130
Because I guess I was like, but thanks for ruining the best day of my life.
因为我当时大概是说，但还是谢谢你毁了我人生中最美好的一天。

907
00:38:17.130 --> 00:38:18.550
Well, that's the worSt.
天哪，那真是太糟糕了。

908
00:38:18.550 --> 00:38:24.850
When you have one or two lines on a show, and there's no like entrance ramp to your performance.
当你在一档节目里只有一两句台词，而且你的表演没有任何铺垫时。

909
00:38:24.850 --> 00:38:28.330
You just have to deliver this one line exactly right.
你必须得把这一句台词说得恰到好处。

910
00:38:28.490 --> 00:38:31.510
And you're on this new set with new people.
而且你身处一个全新的片场，面对着一群陌生人。

911
00:38:31.690 --> 00:38:34.230
And there's all this just adrenaline running through you.
你整个人都处于肾上腺素飙升的状态。

912
00:38:34.630 --> 00:38:36.010
And Suzanne Somers, hi.
还有苏珊·萨默斯，嗨。

913
00:38:36.470 --> 00:38:39.830
I've watched her my whole childhood, whips me around.
我从小看她的戏长大，她一把将我转了过来。

914
00:38:40.310 --> 00:38:44.770
And while I was waiting to do my scene after the director gave me that note in rehearsals,
在导演排练时给了我那个建议后，我等着拍我的戏份，

915
00:38:44.770 --> 00:38:48.410
I literally was in the wings going, thanks for ruining the best day of my life.
我当时真的在侧幕边念叨着，谢谢你毁了我人生中最美好的一天。

916
00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:50.290
Thanks for ruining the best day of my life.
谢谢你毁了我人生中最美好的一天。

917
00:38:50.470 --> 00:38:53.390
Thank you for ruining the best day.
谢谢你毁了这最美好的一天。

918
00:38:53.710 --> 00:38:55.750
That's the other problem when you have one line.
这就是只有一句台词时的另一个问题。

919
00:38:55.910 --> 00:38:59.310
You way overanalyze it so much.
你会过度分析它，想得太多。

920
00:38:59.450 --> 00:39:00.190
I was horrible.
我当时表现得太糟糕了。

921
00:39:00.590 --> 00:39:02.550
Well, Alyssa Preston was amazing.
其实，艾丽莎·普雷斯顿表现得很棒。

922
00:39:02.690 --> 00:39:03.370
She was.
确实是。

923
00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:04.750
Her first TV job.
那是她的第一份电视工作。

924
00:39:04.910 --> 00:39:08.510
She has gone on to work steadily in television and film.
后来她在电视和电影界一直有稳定的工作。

925
00:39:08.690 --> 00:39:11.770
She was in Grey's Anatomy, Modern Family, Jane the Virgin,
她出演过《实习医生格蕾》、《摩登家庭》、《处女情缘》，

926
00:39:11.770 --> 00:39:15.910
the movie Horrible Bosses 2, No Monk, No Law and Order.
还有电影《恶老板2》、没演过《神探阿蒙》和《法律与秩序》。

927
00:39:16.070 --> 00:39:16.610
Comedy.
喜剧。

928
00:39:16.850 --> 00:39:17.930
She's a comedy gal.
她是个喜剧咖。

929
00:39:18.070 --> 00:39:18.750
Comedy gal.
喜剧咖。

930
00:39:19.090 --> 00:39:21.550
Back to the story at hand.
回到正题。

931
00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:29.130
Phyllis has decided to go down and start dancing with Michael while she waits for Bob to join her.
菲利斯决定走下去，在等鲍勃加入她之前，开始和迈克尔跳舞。

932
00:39:29.470 --> 00:39:31.590
Yeah, and she's really getting into it.
没错，她真的很投入。

933
00:39:31.690 --> 00:39:36.670
So much so, she does kind of this pony move and throws out her back.
投入到她跳了一种类似小马舞的动作，结果闪到了腰。

934
00:39:36.670 --> 00:39:43.930
Like, that gasping, sort of bleeped mother effort that she says is not in the shooting draft.
比如，她那声倒吸凉气、被消音的“妈的”之类的词，剧本初稿里并没有。

935
00:39:44.150 --> 00:39:44.430
Really?
真的吗？

936
00:39:44.890 --> 00:39:45.210
Yeah.
是的。

937
00:39:45.370 --> 00:39:50.990
It says that she lets out a yell, you know, but I think that they had fun with that on the day.
剧本上写的是她发出了一声尖叫，你知道的，但我认为他们在拍摄当天玩得很开心。

938
00:39:51.170 --> 00:39:54.550
Can I just say that Phyllis is very good at fake injury?
我能说菲利斯非常擅长假装受伤吗？

939
00:39:54.890 --> 00:39:56.310
I so believed it.
我当时完全信了。

940
00:39:56.390 --> 00:39:57.430
I was worried for her.
我真为她担心。

941
00:39:57.590 --> 00:39:58.070
I know.
我知道。

942
00:39:58.370 --> 00:40:01.490
I mean, she gets her, like, whole face to turn red and stuff.
我是说，她能让整张脸涨得通红之类的。

943
00:40:01.670 --> 00:40:06.050
And, like, everything she does as a person with a back injury was so right on for me.
而且，她作为一个腰部受伤的人所做的一切，在我看来都太真实了。

944
00:40:06.510 --> 00:40:07.870
She's great at physical comedy.
她很擅长肢体喜剧。

945
00:40:08.130 --> 00:40:09.430
I've got a side story.
我有个小插曲要讲。

946
00:40:09.670 --> 00:40:10.010
What?
什么？

947
00:40:10.110 --> 00:40:11.250
I know we just had one.
我知道我们刚讲过一个了。

948
00:40:11.390 --> 00:40:11.670
Uh-oh.
噢，不。

949
00:40:12.070 --> 00:40:14.970
I threw out my back once, just like Phyllis.
我曾经也闪到过腰，就像菲利斯那样。

950
00:40:15.170 --> 00:40:17.610
And it was while I was talking to Christy Brinkley.
而且那还是在我跟克里斯蒂·布林克利说话的时候。

951
00:40:18.210 --> 00:40:18.690
What?
什么？

952
00:40:19.030 --> 00:40:19.270
Yeah.
是啊。

953
00:40:19.830 --> 00:40:20.730
Christy Brinkley.
克里斯蒂·布林克利。

954
00:40:20.810 --> 00:40:22.870
How do you throw out your back while talking?
你怎么会说话的时候闪到腰的？

955
00:40:23.210 --> 00:40:24.370
Phyllis was dancing.
菲利斯当时在跳舞。

956
00:40:24.790 --> 00:40:25.810
Well, I was backstage.
嗯，我当时在后台。

957
00:40:25.810 --> 00:40:27.690
I was doing this game show.
我在录一个游戏节目。

958
00:40:28.730 --> 00:40:31.490
And Christy Brinkley was in the waiting room.
克里斯蒂·布林克利就在候场室里。

959
00:40:31.610 --> 00:40:34.530
She was going to be a guest on the next version of the game show.
她是下一期节目的嘉宾。

960
00:40:34.670 --> 00:40:35.470
You know, the next episode.
你知道的，就是下一集。

961
00:40:36.230 --> 00:40:37.770
I was just so excited.
我当时太激动了。

962
00:40:37.770 --> 00:40:41.150
I mean, to maybe meet Christy Brinkley.
我是说，能见到克里斯蒂·布林克利。

963
00:40:41.330 --> 00:40:42.630
Did you run up or something?
你跑过去还是怎么着？

964
00:40:42.890 --> 00:40:48.510
I threw my arms out in a gesture where I was like, hi, Christy Brinkley.
我张开双臂做了一个手势，就像是说，嗨，克里斯蒂·布林克利。

965
00:40:48.510 --> 00:40:54.770
And in throwing, just gesturing my arms open, I threw out my back.
就在我张开双臂做手势的时候，我闪到了腰。

966
00:40:54.910 --> 00:40:55.950
It was like a pop.
就像“砰”的一声。

967
00:40:56.130 --> 00:40:58.570
It felt like something popped in my back.
感觉背部有什么东西断了。

968
00:40:58.610 --> 00:41:04.410
But I was trying to hold it together because she smiled and she was talking with me.
但我努力强撑着，因为她对我笑了，还在跟我说话。

969
00:41:04.410 --> 00:41:10.470
And I don't know if she could see the pain, like, washing over my eyes and my whole body.
我不知道她有没有看出我眼里的痛苦，那种痛苦蔓延到了我的全身。

970
00:41:10.630 --> 00:41:14.350
And like I said, you know, if Phyllis gets all red, I felt hot.
就像我说的，如果菲利斯脸红了，我当时感觉浑身发烫。

971
00:41:14.570 --> 00:41:16.330
Like, I felt that.
那种感觉，我感受到了。

972
00:41:16.870 --> 00:41:18.390
And then it just seized up.
然后腰就彻底僵住了。

973
00:41:18.470 --> 00:41:19.530
Like, I couldn't even move.
我甚至动弹不得。

974
00:41:19.770 --> 00:41:21.210
They brought the medic in.
他们叫来了医护人员。

975
00:41:21.470 --> 00:41:22.590
On the game show.
在游戏节目现场？

976
00:41:22.590 --> 00:41:23.010
Yes.
是的。

977
00:41:23.210 --> 00:41:26.730
They gave me some ice and some Advil.
他们给了我一些冰袋和布洛芬。

978
00:41:26.930 --> 00:41:34.050
And from there, I had to get loaded in a car to go do this movie in Canada with Ben Stiller and Mike White.
在那之后，我得被抬上车，去加拿大拍一部本·斯蒂勒和迈克·怀特的电影。

979
00:41:34.330 --> 00:41:35.610
It was my dream job.
那是我的梦想工作。

980
00:41:35.730 --> 00:41:36.830
My dream job.
我的梦想工作。

981
00:41:37.030 --> 00:41:40.130
I'm playing Ben Stiller's wife in a Mike White movie.
我在迈克·怀特的电影里演本·斯蒂勒的妻子。

982
00:41:40.390 --> 00:41:41.590
And you couldn't move.
然后你就动不了了。

983
00:41:41.710 --> 00:41:42.410
I couldn't move.
我动不了了。

984
00:41:42.410 --> 00:41:45.510
All because you wanted to show Christy Brinkley a big gesture.
就因为你想给克里斯蒂·布林克利展示一个大大的手势。

985
00:41:45.510 --> 00:41:46.750
That I was excited to meet her.
为了表示我见到她很兴奋。

986
00:41:46.990 --> 00:41:47.290
Hey!
嘿！

987
00:41:47.950 --> 00:41:48.210
Yes!
是的！

988
00:41:48.910 --> 00:41:54.670
When I got to the airport, they had to have a wheelchair load me onto the plane.
当我到达机场时，他们不得不推着轮椅把我送上飞机。

989
00:41:54.790 --> 00:41:55.730
I mean, I really couldn't walk.
我是说，我真的走不了路。

990
00:41:56.010 --> 00:42:02.690
When I got to Canada, they had a doctor meet me at my hotel.
到了加拿大，他们安排了一位医生在酒店见我。

991
00:42:02.850 --> 00:42:03.670
This is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

992
00:42:04.030 --> 00:42:06.350
And the next day, it was a driving scene.
第二天要拍一场开车戏。

993
00:42:06.530 --> 00:42:09.330
My character was supposed to drive and I couldn't do it.
我的角色需要开车，但我做不到。

994
00:42:09.730 --> 00:42:11.990
And I was mortified.
我当时尴尬极了。

995
00:42:12.410 --> 00:42:13.890
I was mortified.
我尴尬极了。

996
00:42:13.890 --> 00:42:17.090
Because, of course, when everybody was like, how did you throw out your back?
因为当然了，当大家问我，你是怎么闪到腰的时候？

997
00:42:17.230 --> 00:42:19.430
And you were like, I just made a hugging gesture.
而你却说，我只是做了一个拥抱的手势。

998
00:42:19.710 --> 00:42:19.930
Yeah.
是啊。

999
00:42:20.150 --> 00:42:21.110
I just went, hey.
我只是说了声，嘿。

1000
00:42:21.590 --> 00:42:24.110
And then I seemed like a Looney Tune.
然后我就看起来像个疯子一样。

1001
00:42:25.430 --> 00:42:26.390
But anyway.
总之。

1002
00:42:26.790 --> 00:42:28.910
You can throw out your back very easily.
你的背很容易闪到。

1003
00:42:29.190 --> 00:42:29.750
You can.
确实。

1004
00:42:30.090 --> 00:42:30.770
Just ask Jenna.
问问珍娜就知道了。

1005
00:42:30.770 --> 00:42:32.230
A lot of stories for me today.
我今天有很多故事要讲。

1006
00:42:32.510 --> 00:42:32.990
Okay.
好的。

1007
00:42:33.350 --> 00:42:35.530
Is this what the shower has done to me?
难道是淋浴间对我做了什么吗？

1008
00:42:35.630 --> 00:42:35.930
Yes.
是的。

1009
00:42:36.030 --> 00:42:38.770
It has opened up my vault of stories.
它打开了我故事的宝库。

1010
00:42:38.790 --> 00:42:39.310
It has.
确实打开了。

1011
00:42:39.310 --> 00:42:48.610
Well, I want you guys to notice while Phyllis is being lowered to the ground by Michael, that black pipe on the wall by the shower does not have any lights on it,
好吧，我想请大家注意，当迈克尔把菲利斯放回地面时，淋浴间墙上的那根黑色管道上没有任何灯光，

1012
00:42:48.650 --> 00:42:49.830
but that will change.
但之后会变。

1013
00:42:50.070 --> 00:42:50.310
Oh.
哦。

1014
00:42:50.830 --> 00:42:52.670
It's not lighted now, but it will be.
现在没亮，但之后会亮的。

1015
00:42:52.810 --> 00:42:53.290
That's right.
没错。

1016
00:42:53.810 --> 00:42:57.770
Michael calls Dwight down to help him get Phyllis back up into the office.
迈克尔叫德怀特下来帮他把菲利斯弄回办公室。

1017
00:42:58.050 --> 00:42:58.710
Or is it Philip?
还是说叫菲利普？

1018
00:42:59.250 --> 00:42:59.910
Is it?
是吗？

1019
00:43:00.630 --> 00:43:01.850
He gets a text.
他收到了一条短信。

1020
00:43:01.990 --> 00:43:05.430
He goes, you said something happened to Philip?
他说，你刚才说菲利普出事了？

1021
00:43:05.650 --> 00:43:08.110
And then he looks at Phyllis and goes, did Philip do this to you?
然后他看着菲利斯说，是菲利普把你弄成这样的吗？

1022
00:43:09.510 --> 00:43:11.390
They are hilarious, the two of them.
他们俩真是太搞笑了。

1023
00:43:11.390 --> 00:43:19.470
Well, this is going to start a whole runner where Dwight is going to be tasked with taking care of Phyllis in the conference room.
好吧，这开启了一个长篇桥段，德怀特被指派去会议室照顾菲利斯。

1024
00:43:19.670 --> 00:43:21.090
They're going to wheel her in there.
他们会把她推进去。

1025
00:43:21.430 --> 00:43:23.270
He's going to shut all the curtains.
他会拉上所有的窗帘。

1026
00:43:23.550 --> 00:43:23.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1027
00:43:24.130 --> 00:43:25.810
And then there's a huge commotion.
然后里面传来一阵巨大的骚动。

1028
00:43:26.190 --> 00:43:28.370
He comes out in just his tank top.
他只穿着背心就出来了。

1029
00:43:28.650 --> 00:43:32.750
I love moments like that because we don't know what happened and they are clearly something.
我喜欢这样的时刻，因为我们不知道发生了什么，但显然发生了什么大事。

1030
00:43:33.610 --> 00:43:41.250
Halstead shared that in addition to being tasked with creating a storyline that used the old Michael Scott Paper Company set,
霍尔斯特德分享说，除了要创作一个利用旧迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司场景的故事线外，

1031
00:43:41.530 --> 00:43:45.330
they also needed a storyline that they could cut away to.
他们还需要一个可以随时切入的故事线。

1032
00:43:45.530 --> 00:43:46.650
They needed somewhere to go.
他们需要一个可以去的地方。

1033
00:43:46.770 --> 00:43:51.470
But that story also had to take place at Dunder Mifflin because we did not have the budget to go anywhere.
但那个故事也必须发生在邓德·米夫林，因为我们没有预算去别的地方。

1034
00:43:51.690 --> 00:43:51.930
Right.
对。

1035
00:43:52.030 --> 00:43:53.130
And we only had four days.
而且我们只有四天时间。

1036
00:43:53.350 --> 00:43:58.570
So this story of Phyllis throwing out her back and Dwight helping her was the solution.
所以菲利斯闪到腰、德怀特帮她这个故事就是解决方案。

1037
00:43:58.570 --> 00:44:05.250
And I love how scripts and stories sometimes evolve out of that just necessity.
我喜欢剧本和故事有时是如何从这种必要性中演变出来的。

1038
00:44:05.770 --> 00:44:07.470
Everyone is concerned about Phyllis.
每个人都很担心菲利斯。

1039
00:44:07.590 --> 00:44:10.290
There's like moaning sounds coming from the conference room.
会议室里传来呻吟声。

1040
00:44:10.630 --> 00:44:13.350
And Angela has a line to Michael where she says,
安吉拉对迈克尔有一句台词，她说，

1041
00:44:13.490 --> 00:44:18.770
Can you please go back to work instead of masterminding these situations wherein we hurt ourselves?
你能回去工作，而不是策划这些让我们受伤的情况吗？

1042
00:44:19.050 --> 00:44:20.750
This line was so hard for me to say.
这句台词我很难说出口。

1043
00:44:21.130 --> 00:44:21.310
Why?
为什么？

1044
00:44:21.690 --> 00:44:23.270
Because I don't speak like that.
因为我平时不那样说话。

1045
00:44:23.390 --> 00:44:27.330
I don't say stop masterminding situations wherein we hurt ourselves.
我不会说停止策划让我们受伤的情况。

1046
00:44:27.870 --> 00:44:28.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1047
00:44:28.570 --> 00:44:30.770
But Angela had a very formal way of speaking.
但安吉拉说话的方式非常正式。

1048
00:44:31.010 --> 00:44:31.430
She did.
确实。

1049
00:44:31.790 --> 00:44:34.170
And it was something that was really important to the writers.
这对编剧来说非常重要。

1050
00:44:34.290 --> 00:44:40.250
They carry it through the whole entire series where she has sort of this clipped formality in her voice.
他们在整个剧集中都贯彻了这一点，她的声音里总有一种刻板的正式感。

1051
00:44:40.710 --> 00:44:43.170
I'm just pointing it out because I had a hard time saying it.
我只是指出来而已，因为我刚才说的时候很费劲。

1052
00:44:44.030 --> 00:44:47.810
To me, a sentence like that is very similar to being a doctor on like a show,
对我来说，那种句子就像是在电视剧里演医生一样，

1053
00:44:47.950 --> 00:44:50.650
but you're not really a doctor and you have to say medical jargon.
但你并不是真正的医生，却还得说那些医学术语。

1054
00:44:50.810 --> 00:44:51.790
I'd never make it.
我肯定做不到。

1055
00:44:52.230 --> 00:44:53.810
Grey's Anatomy, I'd never be able to do it.
《实习医生格蕾》，我绝对演不了。

1056
00:44:53.870 --> 00:44:54.070
No.
不行。

1057
00:44:54.330 --> 00:44:55.090
No, I can't do it.
不，我做不到。

1058
00:44:55.150 --> 00:44:55.710
Can't do it.
真的做不到。

1059
00:44:55.710 --> 00:45:00.610
Well, somehow, Aaron and Kelly are going to wind up down in Cafe Disco.
总之，亚伦和凯莉最后会去迪斯科咖啡馆。

1060
00:45:00.950 --> 00:45:06.730
Aaron presses play on some music and the ladies start dancing.
亚伦按下音乐播放键，女士们开始跳舞。

1061
00:45:07.230 --> 00:45:07.390
Yeah.
没错。

1062
00:45:07.950 --> 00:45:09.390
Do you know what this song was?
你知道这首歌叫什么吗？

1063
00:45:09.810 --> 00:45:11.610
Was it Boyfriend Hangover?
是《男友宿醉》吗？

1064
00:45:11.610 --> 00:45:13.850
Yeah, it's called Boy Hangover.
对，叫《男孩宿醉》。

1065
00:45:13.970 --> 00:45:14.670
Boy Hangover.
《男孩宿醉》。

1066
00:45:14.970 --> 00:45:16.250
Do you know who wrote it?
你知道是谁写的吗？

1067
00:45:16.470 --> 00:45:16.850
No.
不知道。

1068
00:45:17.410 --> 00:45:19.310
Our writer, Lester Lewis.
我们的编剧，莱斯特·刘易斯。

1069
00:45:19.730 --> 00:45:21.310
You are kidding me.
你在开玩笑吧。

1070
00:45:21.450 --> 00:45:21.730
No.
没有。

1071
00:45:21.970 --> 00:45:23.130
I thought it was so catchy.
我觉得这首歌特别洗脑。

1072
00:45:23.470 --> 00:45:26.010
It's sung by this woman named Bonnie McKee.
是由一位叫邦妮·麦基的女士演唱的。

1073
00:45:26.010 --> 00:45:28.670
She's a Grammy-nominated singer-songwriter.
她是一位获得过格莱美提名的创作型歌手。

1074
00:45:28.810 --> 00:45:34.510
She has written number one hits for Britney Spears, Katy Perry, and Tao Cruz.
她为布兰妮·斯皮尔斯、凯蒂·佩里和泰欧·克鲁兹写过冠军单曲。

1075
00:45:34.710 --> 00:45:36.110
I thought we should listen to it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

1076
00:45:36.190 --> 00:45:37.230
Here's Boy Hangover.
这就是《男孩宿醉》。

1077
00:45:41.980 --> 00:45:59.290
How great is it that Lester wrote the lyrics to that song?
莱斯特能写出这首歌的歌词，是不是太棒了？

1078
00:45:59.310 --> 00:45:59.990
It's so good.
真的太好听了。

1079
00:45:59.990 --> 00:46:01.030
I loved the song.
我很喜欢这首歌。

1080
00:46:01.150 --> 00:46:01.890
I thought it was catchy.
我觉得它很抓耳。

1081
00:46:02.110 --> 00:46:04.430
I downloaded it and now I have it.
我下载了，现在我有这首歌了。

1082
00:46:04.770 --> 00:46:07.370
This was one of the songs I was listening to, you know,
这是我一直在听的歌之一，你知道的，

1083
00:46:07.450 --> 00:46:09.910
because I like to stay on theme while working on an episode.
因为我喜欢在制作剧集时保持主题一致。

1084
00:46:10.090 --> 00:46:10.310
Yeah.
没错。

1085
00:46:10.890 --> 00:46:12.230
Well, maybe we should take a break.
好吧，也许我们该休息一下了。

1086
00:46:12.450 --> 00:46:13.530
I want to go eat my yogurt.
我想去吃我的酸奶了。

1087
00:46:13.890 --> 00:46:15.070
It's been on my mind.
我一直惦记着它。

1088
00:46:15.350 --> 00:46:16.290
Honey, I know it.
亲爱的，我懂的。

1089
00:46:16.290 --> 00:46:17.530
If you are okay with that.
如果你没意见的话。

1090
00:46:17.630 --> 00:46:19.490
I saw you eyeing your snack bag.
我看到你一直在盯着你的零食袋看。

1091
00:46:19.650 --> 00:46:20.010
I know.
我知道。

1092
00:46:20.170 --> 00:46:20.730
It's time.
是时候了。

1093
00:46:20.850 --> 00:46:21.350
It's time.
是时候了。

1094
00:46:21.610 --> 00:46:23.270
We'll be back after I eat my yogurt.
等我吃完酸奶我们就回来。

1095
00:46:23.610 --> 00:46:24.090
Okay.
好的。

1096
00:46:33.790 --> 00:46:34.710
We are back.
我们回来了。

1097
00:46:34.890 --> 00:46:35.790
My yogurt was great.
我的酸奶太好吃了。

1098
00:46:36.170 --> 00:46:36.530
Yay.
耶。

1099
00:46:37.090 --> 00:46:40.610
And speaking of eating, Michael is eating his lunch alone.
说到吃，迈克尔正在独自吃午餐。

1100
00:46:40.870 --> 00:46:41.870
Might as well be dinner.
这简直跟吃晚餐差不多了。

1101
00:46:42.150 --> 00:46:43.270
That broke my heart.
那真是让我心碎。

1102
00:46:43.410 --> 00:46:43.970
I know.
我知道。

1103
00:46:44.730 --> 00:46:45.650
So sad.
太难过了。

1104
00:46:45.830 --> 00:46:46.310
Michael.
迈克尔。

1105
00:46:47.250 --> 00:46:49.830
Meanwhile, Phyllis is in the conference room.
与此同时，菲利斯正在会议室里。

1106
00:46:50.390 --> 00:46:55.190
Dwight has started working on her back and Jim is outside collecting flowers.
德怀特开始帮她按摩背部，吉姆在外面采花。

1107
00:46:56.090 --> 00:46:56.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1108
00:46:56.410 --> 00:46:57.110
It's very sweet.
非常贴心。

1109
00:46:57.270 --> 00:46:59.230
He's making a little bouquet for Pam.
他正在为帕姆扎一小束花。

1110
00:46:59.370 --> 00:46:59.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1111
00:47:00.070 --> 00:47:04.430
Jenna, this is on the side of the writer's building where the warehouse was.
珍娜，这是在编剧大楼侧面，也就是仓库所在的地方。

1112
00:47:04.730 --> 00:47:07.550
So automatically I was like, is this 3.30 PM?
所以我当时就想，这是下午三点半吗？

1113
00:47:07.790 --> 00:47:08.110
Yes.
是的。

1114
00:47:08.310 --> 00:47:10.950
Because we learned last week we filmed there at 3.30.
因为我们上周了解到我们是在三点半在那里拍摄的。

1115
00:47:11.570 --> 00:47:13.450
Also, you know those flowers weren't there.
而且，你知道那些花本来是不在那里的。

1116
00:47:13.770 --> 00:47:14.170
No.
没错。

1117
00:47:14.450 --> 00:47:17.590
They had planted them just for the scene so that he could then cut them.
他们是为了这场戏特意种上的，这样他才能去采摘。

1118
00:47:17.590 --> 00:47:19.430
There have never been flowers there.
那里从来没有过花。

1119
00:47:19.590 --> 00:47:19.830
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1120
00:47:19.910 --> 00:47:21.350
Just some weeds, kind of.
只有一些杂草之类的。

1121
00:47:21.530 --> 00:47:21.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1122
00:47:22.090 --> 00:47:23.310
And a giant bug.
还有一只巨大的虫子。

1123
00:47:23.530 --> 00:47:24.470
But that's it.
但仅此而已。

1124
00:47:24.690 --> 00:47:25.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1125
00:47:25.050 --> 00:47:29.890
And then the big bunch of parrots that we had for a small period of time.
还有我们曾养过一小段时间的那一大群鹦鹉。

1126
00:47:30.030 --> 00:47:31.810
And that one rooster across the way.
以及对面那只公鸡。

1127
00:47:32.030 --> 00:47:33.170
But not flowers.
但没有花。

1128
00:47:33.450 --> 00:47:34.310
But not flowers.
确实没有花。

1129
00:47:34.670 --> 00:47:39.670
So they would plant and then replant these flowers so that Jim could collect them.
所以他们会种上这些花，然后再重新种，好让吉姆去采。

1130
00:47:39.670 --> 00:47:41.570
So those were some fakey real flowers.
所以那些是假装成真花的花。

1131
00:47:42.270 --> 00:47:45.750
Meanwhile, Cafe Disco is poppin'.
与此同时，咖啡迪斯科正热闹着呢。

1132
00:47:45.750 --> 00:47:46.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1133
00:47:46.370 --> 00:47:48.310
Aaron has invited a friend, Ashley.
亚伦邀请了一位朋友，阿什利。

1134
00:47:49.110 --> 00:47:54.010
I loved the exchange between Oscar and Aaron when he's like, wait, you invited someone?
我特别喜欢奥斯卡和亚伦之间的那段对话，当时他说，等等，你邀请了别人？

1135
00:47:54.230 --> 00:47:56.170
And Aaron's like, yeah, is that not okay?
亚伦说，是啊，这有什么问题吗？

1136
00:47:56.290 --> 00:47:59.550
And Oscar's like, I mean, I've worked here eight years and I never.
奥斯卡说，我的意思是，我在这里工作八年了，我从来没……

1137
00:47:59.710 --> 00:48:01.850
And then they just run off and he goes, rude.
然后他们就跑开了，他说，真没礼貌。

1138
00:48:03.470 --> 00:48:04.910
I just loved it.
我太喜欢这段了。

1139
00:48:05.270 --> 00:48:09.090
Ashley doesn't have any lines, but she was played by Alexis Teague.
阿什利没有台词，但她是由亚历克西斯·蒂格饰演的。

1140
00:48:09.090 --> 00:48:14.050
And now begins what looks like a dance-off.
现在开始的看起来像是一场斗舞。

1141
00:48:14.250 --> 00:48:15.370
It's full on.
非常激烈。

1142
00:48:15.450 --> 00:48:16.290
It's full on a dance-off.
这完全是一场斗舞。

1143
00:48:16.290 --> 00:48:16.570
Kelly and Andy.
凯莉和安迪。

1144
00:48:16.850 --> 00:48:17.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1145
00:48:17.610 --> 00:48:20.490
We had a fan question from Gianna W.
我们收到一个来自吉安娜·W的粉丝提问。

1146
00:48:21.010 --> 00:48:26.690
The dance-off runner between Andy and Kelly is so great, I personally think they would have made a good couple.
安迪和凯莉之间的斗舞戏太棒了，我个人认为他们会是一对很好的情侣。

1147
00:48:27.010 --> 00:48:28.770
Did the writers ever think of doing that?
编剧们有没有考虑过这样做？

1148
00:48:29.110 --> 00:48:38.330
So I asked Warren about this and he said the writers room pretty much discussed every possible dating scenario for Kelly.
所以我问了沃伦这个问题，他说编剧室几乎讨论过凯莉所有可能的约会对象。

1149
00:48:38.970 --> 00:48:42.810
But Andy and Kelly never made it on one of those note cards and he said, you know what?
但安迪和凯莉从来没出现在那些卡片上，他说，你知道吗？

1150
00:48:42.930 --> 00:48:44.030
That would have been great.
那一定会很棒。

1151
00:48:44.230 --> 00:48:45.350
I wish we would have gone there.
我真希望我们当时去了那里。

1152
00:48:45.630 --> 00:48:47.210
I thought they had great chemistry.
我觉得他们很有默契。

1153
00:48:47.530 --> 00:48:48.130
I did too.
我也是。

1154
00:48:48.170 --> 00:48:49.570
They seem great for each other.
他们看起来真的很般配。

1155
00:48:50.130 --> 00:48:59.730
And I would like you to note at 13 minutes, 54 seconds, at the beginning of the dance-off, red chili pepper lights on the black pipe by the shower.
我想请大家注意在13分54秒，斗舞开始的时候，淋浴间旁边的黑管上挂着红辣椒灯。

1156
00:48:59.950 --> 00:49:00.630
Where did those come from?
那些灯是从哪儿来的？

1157
00:49:00.790 --> 00:49:01.350
I don't know.
我不知道。

1158
00:49:01.470 --> 00:49:04.770
Did Aaron and Kelly like start decorating when they went down there?
是亚伦和凯利下去之后开始装饰的吗？

1159
00:49:04.950 --> 00:49:06.070
Did Ashley bring them?
是阿什莉带来的吗？

1160
00:49:06.990 --> 00:49:08.990
No, Ashley didn't bring them.
不，不是阿什莉带来的。

1161
00:49:09.190 --> 00:49:09.530
Were they there?
它们本来就在那儿吗？

1162
00:49:09.530 --> 00:49:10.210
They were there.
它们本来就在那儿。

1163
00:49:10.410 --> 00:49:11.790
Oh yeah, Ashley just got there.
噢对，阿什莉刚到那儿。

1164
00:49:11.790 --> 00:49:16.210
They weren't there when Phyllis was dancing, but now they're there for the dance-off.
菲利斯跳舞的时候它们还没在，但现在斗舞时它们就在那儿了。

1165
00:49:16.590 --> 00:49:18.650
And Michael is missing all of it.
而且迈克尔错过了这一切。

1166
00:49:18.790 --> 00:49:21.090
He's up in the kitchen being a sad sack.
他正在厨房里垂头丧气呢。

1167
00:49:21.290 --> 00:49:22.550
But he can hear it.
但他能听见。

1168
00:49:22.650 --> 00:49:25.370
He says, I can still hear the music in my head.
他说，我脑子里还能听到音乐。

1169
00:49:25.730 --> 00:49:28.230
Well, Creed is going to exit the bathroom.
嗯，克里德正要从洗手间出来。

1170
00:49:28.410 --> 00:49:29.350
The men's room.
男洗手间。

1171
00:49:29.750 --> 00:49:30.890
While eating chicken.
一边吃着鸡肉。

1172
00:49:31.150 --> 00:49:32.630
I really love that detail.
我真的很喜欢这个细节。

1173
00:49:32.770 --> 00:49:35.950
Halstead mentioned it was one of the little jokes that he loved as well.
哈尔斯特德提到这也是他喜欢的小笑话之一。

1174
00:49:36.090 --> 00:49:37.990
He's full on eating a chicken leg.
他正在大口啃着鸡腿。

1175
00:49:38.210 --> 00:49:38.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1176
00:49:38.450 --> 00:49:39.650
Coming out of the restroom.
从洗手间走出来。

1177
00:49:39.650 --> 00:49:41.990
And Creed's like, I hear it too, Michael.
然后克里德说，我也听到了，迈克尔。

1178
00:49:42.590 --> 00:49:44.590
Creed says, I hear it too, boss.
克里德说，我也听到了，老板。

1179
00:49:44.850 --> 00:49:46.870
Oh yeah, I hear it too, boss.
噢对，我也听到了，老板。

1180
00:49:47.330 --> 00:49:50.070
So Michael's like, oh my gosh, something's happening.
所以迈克尔觉得，天哪，有什么事要发生了。

1181
00:49:50.470 --> 00:49:56.850
And sure enough, he gets down to the cafe disco and it's like happening.
果然，他下到咖啡厅迪斯科现场，发现派对正进行得如火如荼。

1182
00:49:57.150 --> 00:49:57.810
It's a party.
那是个派对。

1183
00:49:58.070 --> 00:49:59.270
There's a limbo pole.
还有根凌波舞杆。

1184
00:49:59.630 --> 00:50:00.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1185
00:50:00.230 --> 00:50:01.190
And I have questions.
我有些疑问。

1186
00:50:01.430 --> 00:50:01.750
Okay.
好的。

1187
00:50:01.950 --> 00:50:02.990
Because it's so great.
因为这太棒了。

1188
00:50:03.030 --> 00:50:06.990
You see two people walk in and they have to like, you know, limbo under.
你看到两个人走进来，他们得，你知道，从下面钻过去。

1189
00:50:07.410 --> 00:50:08.530
Meredith does a shimmy.
梅雷迪思扭动着身体钻了过去。

1190
00:50:08.530 --> 00:50:12.050
Your character walks in and just walks under it.
你的角色走进来，直接就从下面走过去了。

1191
00:50:12.170 --> 00:50:13.250
Just straight under it.
就这么直直地走过去了。

1192
00:50:13.310 --> 00:50:13.930
No problem.
没问题。

1193
00:50:14.130 --> 00:50:15.150
Didn't have to bend at all.
根本不需要弯腰。

1194
00:50:15.410 --> 00:50:16.430
Who wrote that joke?
这个笑话是谁写的？

1195
00:50:16.930 --> 00:50:20.970
Well, I asked Warren and Halstead and they both were like, it was Warren.
嗯，我问了沃伦和哈尔斯特德，他们都说是沃伦写的。

1196
00:50:21.170 --> 00:50:23.430
Warren was like, yeah, that was me.
沃伦说，是啊，那是我写的。

1197
00:50:24.010 --> 00:50:25.370
Well, it's hilarious to me.
嗯，我觉得这太搞笑了。

1198
00:50:25.450 --> 00:50:29.250
This is my ex-husband's joke because he clearly knows I'm a short stack.
这是我前夫写的笑话，因为他显然知道我是个矮个子。

1199
00:50:29.730 --> 00:50:31.110
Well, how did you do it?
那么，你是怎么做到的？

1200
00:50:31.190 --> 00:50:34.250
Did they bring you down and measure you to set the pole?
他们是不是把你叫过去量了身高才设置的杆子高度？

1201
00:50:34.250 --> 00:50:35.030
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1202
00:50:35.270 --> 00:50:38.210
They duct taped that pole to the wall, right?
他们用大力胶把那根杆子粘在墙上了，对吧？

1203
00:50:38.370 --> 00:50:39.390
That everyone walked under.
就是大家都从下面走过的那根。

1204
00:50:39.550 --> 00:50:40.230
It's like a broom.
它看起来像把扫帚。

1205
00:50:40.410 --> 00:50:41.850
It's meant to look like a broom handle.
它本来就是想做成扫帚柄的样子。

1206
00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:42.190
Right.
没错。

1207
00:50:42.430 --> 00:50:44.830
And I had to practice walking under it.
我还得练习从它下面走过去。

1208
00:50:45.150 --> 00:50:48.050
I, on purpose this episode, I wear flats.
这一集我特意穿了平底鞋。

1209
00:50:48.110 --> 00:50:50.150
My character never wears flats.
我的角色从不穿平底鞋。

1210
00:50:50.310 --> 00:50:52.470
My character is always in three inch heels.
我的角色总是穿着三英寸的高跟鞋。

1211
00:50:52.910 --> 00:50:56.310
This entire episode, I had on little tiny flats.
整整这一集，我都穿着小小的平底鞋。

1212
00:50:56.850 --> 00:50:57.350
Wow.
哇。

1213
00:50:57.590 --> 00:50:59.970
This is the shoe thing you were mentioning earlier.
这就是你刚才提到的鞋子的问题吧。

1214
00:50:59.970 --> 00:51:01.590
Yes, I'll put it in stories.
是的，我会把它发到快拍里。

1215
00:51:01.790 --> 00:51:08.150
I took a screen grab of them and I did ever so slightly, guys, have to tilt my head, just
我截了张图，伙计们，我稍微，真的只是稍微歪了歪头，

1216
00:51:08.150 --> 00:51:11.430
very tiny, but I could walk right under that pole.
非常轻微，但我可以直接从那根杆子下面走过去。

1217
00:51:11.750 --> 00:51:12.690
It was so funny.
太好笑了。

1218
00:51:12.910 --> 00:51:17.090
I'm the person, guys, when your plane lands and everyone stands up and they're waiting
伙计们，我就是那种人，当飞机降落，大家都在起身等待时，

1219
00:51:17.090 --> 00:51:22.030
and everyone has to duck because the overhead compartments, you know, when you are still
每个人都得低着头，因为行李架，你知道，当你还坐在座位上，

1220
00:51:22.030 --> 00:51:25.350
at your seat, you haven't been able to get in the aisle because there's so many people
还没法走到过道里，因为有太多人在拿他们的东西，

1221
00:51:25.350 --> 00:51:26.250
getting their stuff.
你得低着头。

1222
00:51:26.390 --> 00:51:26.610
Yep.
没错。

1223
00:51:26.790 --> 00:51:29.230
I can stand fully upright under the overhead.
我可以在行李架下完全站直。

1224
00:51:29.230 --> 00:51:30.650
That must feel so good.
那感觉一定很棒。

1225
00:51:30.910 --> 00:51:31.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1226
00:51:31.370 --> 00:51:34.730
I just look at all these people hunched over while they're waiting to get off a plane.
我看着那些人弯着腰等下飞机，

1227
00:51:34.910 --> 00:51:36.070
I got no problem.
我完全没压力。

1228
00:51:37.810 --> 00:51:40.250
But don't ask you to get something off the top shelf.
但别指望你能从顶层架子上拿东西。

1229
00:51:40.510 --> 00:51:40.950
No.
没错。

1230
00:51:41.410 --> 00:51:43.330
Why would I put anything on the top shelf?
我为什么要往顶层架子上放东西呢？

1231
00:51:43.570 --> 00:51:44.230
You don't.
你确实不会。

1232
00:51:44.570 --> 00:51:48.770
The only reason Angela is there is to get some signatures on a piece of paper and Michael
安吉拉去那儿的唯一原因就是为了让迈克尔在纸上签名，而迈克尔

1233
00:51:48.770 --> 00:51:51.810
says he's only going to give her one signature per song.
说他每唱一首歌才肯签一个名。

1234
00:51:51.810 --> 00:51:59.150
And Angela, you have this line where you say, I don't like the general spirit of music.
安吉拉，你有一句台词说：“我不喜欢音乐的大体精神。”

1235
00:51:59.450 --> 00:52:02.790
My character says, look, I hate to be that person.
我的角色说，听着，我不想做那种人。

1236
00:52:03.150 --> 00:52:03.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1237
00:52:03.830 --> 00:52:06.290
But I just don't like the general spirit of music.
但我就是不喜欢音乐的大体精神。

1238
00:52:06.850 --> 00:52:13.010
Renee from Fargo, North Dakota would like to know who wrote that line, she loves it.
来自北达科他州法戈的蕾妮想知道是谁写了那句台词，她超爱那句。

1239
00:52:13.010 --> 00:52:18.610
So we asked Warren and Halstead this question, and Warren said it's probably his favorite
所以我们问了沃伦和霍尔斯特德这个问题，沃伦说这可能是他最喜欢的问题，

1240
00:52:18.610 --> 00:52:20.670
question because he loves that line too.
因为他也超爱那句台词。

1241
00:52:20.990 --> 00:52:27.630
He shared that he and Halstead were writing together on a short-lived show for the WB called
他分享说，他和霍尔斯特德曾一起为华纳兄弟电视台一部短命的剧集写剧本，剧名叫

1242
00:52:27.630 --> 00:52:31.610
Modern Men, starring Jane Seymour and Max Greenfield.
《现代男人》，由简·西摩和马克斯·格林菲尔德主演。

1243
00:52:31.750 --> 00:52:36.370
And in one of the episodes, one of the guys is trying to break up with his drab girlfriend
在其中一集里，有个男人正试图和他的乏味女友分手，

1244
00:52:36.370 --> 00:52:39.110
played by guest actor Arden Mirren.
由客串演员雅顿·米伦饰演。

1245
00:52:39.110 --> 00:52:39.970
Oh, I love her.
噢，我超爱她。

1246
00:52:40.110 --> 00:52:40.810
She's hilarious.
她太搞笑了。

1247
00:52:41.290 --> 00:52:41.590
She's so funny.
她真的很有趣。

1248
00:52:42.150 --> 00:52:44.050
Warren said she was amazingly funny.
沃伦说她简直太搞笑了。

1249
00:52:44.310 --> 00:52:48.190
And Halstead and Warren had pitched a line that she hates music.
霍尔斯特德和沃伦当时提议了一句台词，说她讨厌音乐。

1250
00:52:48.590 --> 00:52:53.470
And what Arden's character said was, not a fan, like about music.
而雅顿的角色说的是，不太感冒，就是关于音乐的那种。

1251
00:52:53.750 --> 00:52:53.890
Yeah.
没错。

1252
00:52:54.070 --> 00:52:56.430
And they said that Arden killed it, and it was really funny.
他们说Arden演得特别好，而且真的非常搞笑。

1253
00:52:56.590 --> 00:53:00.730
And when they went to write this episode, they really could see Angela identifying with
当他们写这一集的时候，他们真的能看出Angela对那种感觉的共鸣，

1254
00:53:00.730 --> 00:53:03.790
that, and they borrowed their own line and added a little tweak.
于是他们借用了自己的台词，并做了一点小小的改动。

1255
00:53:04.110 --> 00:53:08.990
I think it is such an amazing character trait for a person to just be like,
我觉得一个人能直接说出这种话，真的是一种很棒的性格特征，

1256
00:53:09.110 --> 00:53:10.110
I don't get music.
我不懂音乐。

1257
00:53:10.450 --> 00:53:11.350
Yeah, I'm not a fan.
是啊，我不太感冒。

1258
00:53:12.430 --> 00:53:14.590
I'm not a big music person myself.
我自己也不是个音乐迷。

1259
00:53:14.910 --> 00:53:18.090
I know this about you, Jenna, because when we went on our writer's retreat,
Jenna，这一点我很了解你，因为当我们去参加编剧静修会时，

1260
00:53:18.350 --> 00:53:20.630
you were very concentrated on our meal plan.
你非常专注于我们的餐饮计划。

1261
00:53:20.630 --> 00:53:22.170
What were we going to be eating?
我们打算吃什么？

1262
00:53:22.510 --> 00:53:22.690
Yes.
没错。

1263
00:53:22.690 --> 00:53:25.690
And I said something like, what about a playlist for the car ride?
当时我说，要不要在车上放个播放列表？

1264
00:53:25.690 --> 00:53:26.750
And you're like, yeah, I don't care.
结果你说，行啊，我无所谓。

1265
00:53:27.010 --> 00:53:32.290
I don't know if this is why, but the car that I drove out to LA,
我不知道是不是因为这个原因，但我开车去洛杉矶的时候，

1266
00:53:32.290 --> 00:53:36.730
it had no air conditioning and no working radio.
那辆车既没有空调，收音机也坏了。

1267
00:53:37.210 --> 00:53:38.510
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1268
00:53:38.670 --> 00:53:42.210
You were driving in a car with no music on a road trip?
你开车去公路旅行的时候竟然不听音乐？

1269
00:53:42.450 --> 00:53:42.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1270
00:53:43.090 --> 00:53:47.930
And I also had this car in college, and my college was three hours from my hometown.
我在大学时也开过这辆车，我的大学离家乡有三个小时的车程。

1271
00:53:47.930 --> 00:53:53.790
And so I would often drive very, very, very long distances in silence.
所以我经常在极其漫长的旅途中保持沉默。

1272
00:53:54.170 --> 00:53:54.670
Jenna.
Jenna。

1273
00:53:54.670 --> 00:54:00.790
Or I sometimes did bring like an old-fashioned cassette player.
或者我有时会带个老式的卡带播放器。

1274
00:54:00.930 --> 00:54:02.110
And hit play, I hope.
而且还得记得按播放键，希望如此。

1275
00:54:02.250 --> 00:54:04.250
Yeah, I could play off of that.
是啊，我可以用那个听。

1276
00:54:04.330 --> 00:54:08.770
But I got really conditioned to driving without sound.
但我已经习惯了在没有声音的情况下开车。

1277
00:54:08.770 --> 00:54:17.910
And now I listen to news or podcasts, but I just never kind of got into playlists or music.
现在我会听新闻或播客，但我从来没怎么接触过播放列表或音乐。

1278
00:54:17.910 --> 00:54:20.370
I find it like, I don't know.
我觉得它……我也不知道该怎么说。

1279
00:54:20.750 --> 00:54:22.230
I do like music.
我其实喜欢音乐。

1280
00:54:22.450 --> 00:54:23.510
Like, I have whole albuMs.
比如，我有很多完整的专辑。

1281
00:54:23.650 --> 00:54:25.210
I have Sounds of Scranton, you know?
我有《斯克兰顿之声》，你知道吧？

1282
00:54:25.250 --> 00:54:25.470
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1283
00:54:25.470 --> 00:54:29.530
Like, I use music a lot when I'm formulating a character, which is so interesting.
我在塑造角色时经常会用到音乐，这很有意思。

1284
00:54:29.770 --> 00:54:35.010
Because if you had to formulate the character of Jenna Fisher, you would have no music.
因为如果你要塑造Jenna Fisher这个角色，那她肯定是不听音乐的。

1285
00:54:35.270 --> 00:54:36.990
You'd have no music, but good food.
没有音乐，但有美食。

1286
00:54:38.010 --> 00:54:40.330
Yeah, I mean, I love a combo.
是啊，我是说，我喜欢这种组合。

1287
00:54:40.530 --> 00:54:42.950
I love a playlist for a road trip.
我喜欢公路旅行时有播放列表。

1288
00:54:42.950 --> 00:54:46.070
But then I like to turn it off and talk, you know, because I'm chatty.
但之后我喜欢关掉音乐聊天，你知道的，因为我很爱说话。

1289
00:54:46.070 --> 00:54:49.150
My mom always says the best place to talk is in the car.
我妈妈总是说，聊天最好的地方就是在车里。

1290
00:54:49.450 --> 00:54:52.130
That's why I love to do school pickup and drop off.
所以我很喜欢负责接送孩子上下学。

1291
00:54:52.250 --> 00:54:54.050
I feel like my kids are super chatty.
我觉得我的孩子们特别健谈。

1292
00:54:54.210 --> 00:54:54.650
Yeah.
没错。

1293
00:54:55.130 --> 00:54:55.930
Talking about their day.
聊聊他们一天发生的事。

1294
00:54:56.290 --> 00:54:56.530
Right after school.
就在放学之后。

1295
00:54:56.730 --> 00:54:57.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1296
00:54:57.390 --> 00:54:59.150
But my husband loves a playliSt.
但我丈夫很喜欢播放列表。

1297
00:54:59.410 --> 00:55:01.850
And he makes a playlist for every road trip we take.
我们每次去公路旅行他都会制作一个播放列表。

1298
00:55:01.970 --> 00:55:05.410
And it's really cute because the kids now are so connected to it.
这真的很可爱，因为孩子们现在对它很有感情。

1299
00:55:05.570 --> 00:55:10.110
So we were listening a lot to the Red Hot Chili Peppers when we went up to the mountains in Big Bear.
所以我们去大熊山的时候，一直在听呛辣红椒乐队的歌。

1300
00:55:10.410 --> 00:55:13.750
And Jack will say, whenever they come on now, he's like, that's Big Bear.
现在只要他们的歌一响，Jack就会说，那是大熊山。

1301
00:55:13.750 --> 00:55:17.310
You know, my kids and Lee are very connected to music.
你知道，我的孩子们和李都和音乐有着很深的渊源。

1302
00:55:17.490 --> 00:55:18.550
And they do the same thing.
他们也做同样的事情。

1303
00:55:18.570 --> 00:55:20.670
And we have those same things.
我们也有同样的经历。

1304
00:55:21.010 --> 00:55:24.190
Well, like Vampire Weekend for us was like the summer of 2019.
比如对我们来说，Vampire Weekend乐队就像是2019年夏天的代名词。

1305
00:55:24.270 --> 00:55:25.590
That's Vampire Weekend.
那就是Vampire Weekend。

1306
00:55:25.730 --> 00:55:27.490
White Stripes, Seven Nation Army.
白线条乐队的《七国军》。

1307
00:55:27.770 --> 00:55:28.230
Love it.
我很喜欢。

1308
00:55:28.390 --> 00:55:32.410
We would listen to that song as we were driving up to go skiing in Santa Fe.
我们以前开车去圣达菲滑雪时总会听这首歌。

1309
00:55:32.550 --> 00:55:32.850
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1310
00:55:32.950 --> 00:55:35.850
So whenever I hear that song, I just feel the snowy mountain.
所以每当我听到这首歌，我就感觉置身于雪山之中。

1311
00:55:36.130 --> 00:55:37.310
I'm going to Wichita.
我要去威奇托了。

1312
00:55:37.750 --> 00:55:38.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1313
00:55:38.350 --> 00:55:39.310
It's so good.
太棒了。

1314
00:55:39.450 --> 00:55:39.890
So good.
真的太棒了。

1315
00:55:39.890 --> 00:55:45.230
Oh, can I take us into the conference room with Dwight and Phyllis?
噢，我能带大家去看看德怀特和菲利斯在会议室的那段吗？

1316
00:55:45.450 --> 00:55:47.470
Where he's treating her like livestock?
就是他把她当牲口对待的那段？

1317
00:55:47.830 --> 00:55:51.210
And he's rubbing otter oil into her back.
他还在往她背上抹水獭油。

1318
00:55:51.370 --> 00:55:52.470
Yeah, and giving her a carrot.
对，还喂她吃胡萝卜。

1319
00:55:52.810 --> 00:55:56.010
I thought for sure this otter oil thing was made up.
我本来以为这水獭油肯定是编出来的。

1320
00:55:56.170 --> 00:55:57.030
Is it real?
那是真的吗？

1321
00:55:57.530 --> 00:56:02.950
Lady, otter glands can be purchased.
女士，水獭腺体是可以买到的。

1322
00:56:03.330 --> 00:56:05.370
Oh, how do they get them?
噢，他们是怎么弄到的？

1323
00:56:05.690 --> 00:56:07.230
Well, from dead otters.
嗯，从死水獭身上。

1324
00:56:07.230 --> 00:56:07.630
Okay.
好吧。

1325
00:56:07.630 --> 00:56:09.530
They take their anal glands.
他们取走它们的肛门腺。

1326
00:56:09.550 --> 00:56:10.190
Oh, Lord.
噢，天哪。

1327
00:56:10.530 --> 00:56:15.010
And they grind them up and they age them and then they preserve them.
然后把它们磨碎、陈化，再进行防腐处理。

1328
00:56:15.230 --> 00:56:16.510
Who thought of that?
谁想出这种主意的？

1329
00:56:16.670 --> 00:56:19.290
Who thought it was like, save that otter's ass?
谁会想到说，把那只水獭的屁股留着？

1330
00:56:19.390 --> 00:56:20.290
I don't know.
我不知道。

1331
00:56:20.290 --> 00:56:22.830
There's some stuff in there I need to grind up.
我那儿还有些东西需要磨碎。

1332
00:56:23.030 --> 00:56:26.210
You can get one ounce for about eight bucks.
你花八块钱左右就能买到一盎司。

1333
00:56:26.790 --> 00:56:29.670
On another website, I saw you could get it for six.
我在另一个网站上看到六块钱就能买到。

1334
00:56:29.910 --> 00:56:32.010
So if you're in the market, shop around.
所以如果你有需求，记得货比三家。

1335
00:56:32.210 --> 00:56:33.610
Well, what do people use it for?
那人们用它来做什么呢？

1336
00:56:33.830 --> 00:56:35.450
That's what I wanted to know.
这也是我想知道的。

1337
00:56:35.450 --> 00:56:38.910
I guess you use it to lure an otter.
我猜你是用它来引诱水獭。

1338
00:56:39.210 --> 00:56:43.890
You lure an otter with their own anal glands crushed up?
你用它们自己被磨碎的肛门腺去引诱水獭？

1339
00:56:43.990 --> 00:56:46.570
Yeah, with the scent of their own anal glands.
对，用它们自己肛门腺的气味。

1340
00:56:47.210 --> 00:56:47.850
Why?
为什么？

1341
00:56:47.850 --> 00:56:48.810
Exactly.
问得好。

1342
00:56:49.130 --> 00:56:51.310
Why am I luring an otter?
我为什么要引诱水獭？

1343
00:56:51.830 --> 00:56:53.650
I guess hunting.
我猜是为了狩猎。

1344
00:56:54.350 --> 00:56:58.070
But it's just for sport because you don't really use them for anything.
但这只是为了消遣，因为你根本用不上它们。

1345
00:56:58.230 --> 00:57:00.990
You don't use their fur or you don't eat them.
你不用它们的皮毛，也不吃它们。

1346
00:57:01.230 --> 00:57:05.550
You just, I guess, sprinkle their anal glands and then kill them.
我猜你只是撒上它们的肛门腺，然后把它们杀了。

1347
00:57:05.730 --> 00:57:06.030
Why?
为什么？

1348
00:57:06.570 --> 00:57:07.490
This is horrible.
这太可怕了。

1349
00:57:07.910 --> 00:57:12.770
Well, there's a whole market for this sort of like...
嗯，这确实有一个完整的市场，就像是……

1350
00:57:12.770 --> 00:57:14.610
Surely there's something we don't know.
肯定还有些我们不知道的事情。

1351
00:57:14.870 --> 00:57:15.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

1352
00:57:16.030 --> 00:57:18.850
But there's like a lot of gland.
但那儿好像有很多腺体。

1353
00:57:19.530 --> 00:57:24.010
You can buy a lot of glands of different animals for this purpose of luring them.
你可以买到很多不同动物的腺体，用来引诱它们。

1354
00:57:24.350 --> 00:57:27.910
So basically, these animals smell their own...
所以基本上，这些动物闻到它们自己的……

1355
00:57:27.910 --> 00:57:31.630
And I guess they think it's another otter and they come out to say hi.
我想它们以为那是另一只水獭，就出来打招呼了。

1356
00:57:32.170 --> 00:57:32.730
Terrible.
太可怕了。

1357
00:57:32.930 --> 00:57:35.150
This is like Bambi all over again for me.
这对我来说简直就像重温《小鹿斑比》一样。

1358
00:57:35.150 --> 00:57:35.690
I know.
我知道。

1359
00:57:36.430 --> 00:57:40.890
And no references to rubbing it into someone's back for an injury.
而且别提什么把那玩意儿抹在别人背上治伤的事。

1360
00:57:41.390 --> 00:57:45.290
I just want to say if Phyllis went out to the woods, she would be very popular.
我只想说，如果菲利斯去树林里，她会非常受欢迎。

1361
00:57:45.390 --> 00:57:46.970
It'd be like a Snow White moment for her.
对她来说那就像白雪公主的时刻一样。

1362
00:57:47.130 --> 00:57:49.890
She would have a lot of otters coming to say hi.
会有很多水獭跑来跟她打招呼。

1363
00:57:50.550 --> 00:57:52.390
So Dwight and the Shrutes could kill them.
然后德怀特和施鲁特一家就能把它们杀了。

1364
00:57:52.510 --> 00:57:53.430
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1365
00:57:53.670 --> 00:57:56.410
But that is some information I found.
不过这就是我找到的一些信息。

1366
00:57:56.590 --> 00:58:00.370
I'm confused by all of that information, but thank you for sharing it.
我被这些信息搞糊涂了，但还是谢谢你的分享。

1367
00:58:00.490 --> 00:58:01.030
You're welcome.
不客气。

1368
00:58:01.330 --> 00:58:01.730
Okay.
好的。

1369
00:58:01.730 --> 00:58:05.590
There is a full-on dance competition happening now.
现在正在进行一场全面的舞蹈比赛。

1370
00:58:05.850 --> 00:58:07.090
There sure is.
确实是。

1371
00:58:07.230 --> 00:58:09.810
And we got mail from Alexis W.
我们收到了来自澳大利亚的亚历克西斯·W的来信，

1372
00:58:10.050 --> 00:58:11.530
in Australia who said,
她说，

1373
00:58:11.730 --> 00:58:17.470
I have to know if the dance competition between Andy and Kelly was freestyle or scripted.
我必须知道安迪和凯莉之间的舞蹈比赛是即兴的还是有剧本的。

1374
00:58:17.850 --> 00:58:19.690
Lady, I went to the script.
女士，我看了剧本。

1375
00:58:19.990 --> 00:58:21.150
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1376
00:58:21.370 --> 00:58:23.310
It is fully scripted.
它是完全照剧本演的。

1377
00:58:23.450 --> 00:58:25.370
I'm going to read you the descriptions.
我要给你们读一下描述。

1378
00:58:25.950 --> 00:58:30.210
Here is Andy's dance-off description of the script.
这是剧本中对安迪斗舞的描述。

1379
00:58:30.750 --> 00:58:39.010
Andy takes a chair and hops over the back of it, turns around, does a fret-a-stair walk over it so that the chair's back falls to the ground.
安迪拿了一把椅子，从椅背上跳过去，转过身，做了一个跨步动作，把椅背弄倒在地。

1380
00:58:39.230 --> 00:58:45.930
He picks it up, sits on it, and spins on it in a Bob Fosse fashion, flashing jazz hands.
他捡起椅子，坐在上面，像鲍勃·福斯那样旋转，并做出爵士舞的手势。

1381
00:58:46.210 --> 00:58:52.290
He then throws one leg over the back of the chair, gets up, picks up the chair, and pretends that the chair is attacking him,
然后他把一条腿跨过椅背，站起来，拿起椅子，假装椅子在攻击他，

1382
00:58:52.370 --> 00:58:54.850
and then pretends to be killed by the chair.
接着假装被椅子杀死了。

1383
00:58:55.090 --> 00:58:59.350
He gets up and eyes Kelly like, try to top that.
他站起来，盯着凯莉，那眼神仿佛在说，有本事你超越这个。

1384
00:59:00.710 --> 00:59:02.370
Kelly's description is this.
凯莉的描述是这样的。

1385
00:59:02.610 --> 00:59:04.970
Kelly walks over to the shower area.
凯莉走到淋浴区。

1386
00:59:05.130 --> 00:59:10.410
She pretends to turn on the shower and mimes getting wet and lathering herself with soap.
她假装打开淋浴，模仿被水淋湿和用肥皂擦洗身体的样子。

1387
00:59:10.570 --> 00:59:11.210
Oh, my.
天哪。

1388
00:59:11.390 --> 00:59:14.910
She then walks to the chair, which is next to where Andy stands.
然后她走到安迪旁边的椅子那里。

1389
00:59:15.310 --> 00:59:23.270
She stops at the chair, turns like a runway model, winks at Andy, picks up the chair, and walks back to the shower area with it.
她在椅子旁停下，像T台模特一样转身，对安迪眨了眨眼，拿起椅子，带着它走回淋浴区。

1390
00:59:23.270 --> 00:59:29.270
She sits down, arches her back, a la Flashdance, and pretends to be drenched by the shower.
她坐下来，像《闪电舞》里那样拱起背，假装被淋浴的水淋透了。

1391
00:59:29.630 --> 00:59:32.370
She whips her hair around her head in a frenzy.
她疯狂地甩动着头发。

1392
00:59:32.710 --> 00:59:34.990
Then Kelly starts crunking.
然后凯莉开始跳起克朗克舞。

1393
00:59:35.410 --> 00:59:35.650
Okay.
好的。

1394
00:59:36.110 --> 00:59:37.270
That's a dance move.
那是一种舞蹈动作。

1395
00:59:37.430 --> 00:59:39.210
She's putting all her best stuff out there.
她拿出了她所有的看家本领。

1396
00:59:39.370 --> 00:59:40.110
She is.
确实是。

1397
00:59:40.110 --> 00:59:46.590
Well, you might notice that the way it is described is not exactly how you end up seeing it in the show,
嗯，你们可能注意到了，剧本里的描述和你们在剧中最终看到的并不完全一样，

1398
00:59:46.730 --> 00:59:54.330
and that is because Randy did hire a choreographer, and the choreographer's job was to interpret the script
这是因为兰迪确实聘请了一位编舞，编舞的工作是解读剧本，

1399
00:59:54.330 --> 00:59:58.650
and then work with the actors to come up with their moves.
然后与演员合作，构思出他们的动作。

1400
00:59:58.650 --> 01:00:06.590
Randy said our choreographer's name was Mary Ann Kellogg, and she came to us via recommendation from our first AD, Kelly Cantley.
兰迪说我们的编舞名叫玛丽·安·凯洛格，她是经我们的第一副导演凯莉·坎特利推荐而来的。

1401
01:00:07.050 --> 01:00:10.730
Randy said she was absolutely superb and really got this scene.
兰迪说她表现得非常出色，而且真的领悟了这场戏。

1402
01:00:11.110 --> 01:00:16.890
And Warren said they had to use a good choreographer because if the actors had just freestyled the whole time,
沃伦说他们必须请一位优秀的编舞，因为如果演员全程即兴发挥的话，

1403
01:00:17.290 --> 01:00:19.490
it would have been impossible to edit.
剪辑起来是不可能的。

1404
01:00:19.830 --> 01:00:26.070
So although Mindy and Ed brought a lot of ideas for what they would do, this was a planned out dance-off.
所以尽管敏迪和埃德为他们的动作贡献了很多想法，但这其实是一场精心编排的斗舞。

1405
01:00:26.070 --> 01:00:26.830
Yeah.
没错。

1406
01:00:27.090 --> 01:00:30.710
Sort of based loosely on the script, it seeMs.
看起来是大致基于剧本的。

1407
01:00:31.110 --> 01:00:31.910
But it morphed.
但它发生了变化。

1408
01:00:31.930 --> 01:00:34.850
It evolved in this rehearsal process.
它在排练过程中不断演变。

1409
01:00:35.230 --> 01:00:42.050
And Halstead said he definitely remembers them pitching that flash dance moment, and that made it in.
霍尔斯特德说他清楚地记得他们提议加入那个《闪电舞》的桥段，最后也确实用上了。

1410
01:00:42.210 --> 01:00:48.870
You know, something else that Randy shared with us was that we were not listening to music during this.
你知道吗，兰迪还跟我们分享了一件事，那就是我们在拍摄这段戏时并没有听音乐。

1411
01:00:48.990 --> 01:00:51.330
They were using what's called a thump track.
他们用的是所谓的“节拍音轨”。

1412
01:00:51.770 --> 01:01:00.270
Again, for editing purposes, they would just have this speaker that would play like the sort of baseline beat of the song
同样是为了剪辑方便，他们会放一个扬声器，播放歌曲的基准节拍，

1413
01:01:01.030 --> 01:01:03.230
so that the actors would be on tempo.
这样演员们就能跟上节奏。

1414
01:01:04.410 --> 01:01:07.590
But for editing purposes, they put the song on later.
但为了剪辑效果，他们是后期才把歌曲加进去的。

1415
01:01:07.830 --> 01:01:08.310
I know.
我知道。

1416
01:01:08.410 --> 01:01:09.950
So these guys are doing this whole thing.
所以这些人是在这种情况下完成了整段表演。

1417
01:01:10.050 --> 01:01:10.510
You were there.
你当时也在场。

1418
01:01:10.610 --> 01:01:11.410
Was it so crazy?
当时是不是特别疯狂？

1419
01:01:11.630 --> 01:01:12.570
It was so crazy.
确实特别疯狂。

1420
01:01:12.570 --> 01:01:20.190
And also, this is not about the dance-off, but I could always really tell when there was no music when Ellie was dancing.
还有，这虽然跟斗舞无关，但我总能一眼看出艾莉跳舞时没有音乐伴奏。

1421
01:01:21.330 --> 01:01:25.390
Because Ellie just kind of does these jabs and kind of runs in place.
因为艾莉跳的时候总是做些刺拳动作，或者原地小跑。

1422
01:01:25.390 --> 01:01:28.170
Like not at all to what the beat of the song was that's playing.
完全跟播放的歌曲节奏对不上。

1423
01:01:28.330 --> 01:01:32.630
But there was one little moment in the background, I start to tidy up.
不过背景里有一个小细节，我开始收拾东西了。

1424
01:01:32.970 --> 01:01:33.410
Yes.
是的。

1425
01:01:33.650 --> 01:01:35.770
