那挺好的。

1557
01:07:03.150 --> 01:07:06.850
Maybe she was like, I don't even know where to begin, so just do what you're doing.
也许她当时想的是，我甚至不知道从哪开始教，所以你就按你自己的方式跳吧。

1558
01:07:08.150 --> 01:07:13.610
Well, I'll say, I loved shooting these dance scenes.
嗯，我得说，我超爱拍这些舞蹈戏份。

1559
01:07:13.890 --> 01:07:16.470
I was so happy to finally be down in the disco.
终于能去迪斯科舞厅我太开心了。

1560
01:07:17.030 --> 01:07:20.190
But lady, I love a dance party.
但说真的，我超爱舞会。

1561
01:07:20.410 --> 01:07:21.330
I know you do.
我知道你爱。

1562
01:07:21.570 --> 01:07:24.390
And I will stay on the dance floor the whole time at your wedding.
你婚礼的时候，我绝对会全程待在舞池里。

1563
01:07:24.810 --> 01:07:26.930
I want to be out on that dance floor.
我想去舞池里跳个痛快。

1564
01:07:27.210 --> 01:07:32.030
You know, for my 30th birthday, I had a dance party, and I danced the whole time.
你知道吗，我三十岁生日时办了场舞会，我全程都在跳舞。

1565
01:07:32.030 --> 01:07:37.450
And my 50th is going to be coming up in a few years, and I want a dance party again.
再过几年我就要五十岁了，我还想再办一场舞会。

1566
01:07:37.670 --> 01:07:39.390
You should have a dance party.
你应该办一场舞会。

1567
01:07:39.650 --> 01:07:41.590
And I maybe should put on the invitation.
而且我可能得在请柬上写上。

1568
01:07:42.150 --> 01:07:43.310
Wear comfy shoes.
穿双舒服的鞋子。

1569
01:07:43.610 --> 01:07:47.070
And I may not talk to you because I'm going to be dancing the whole time, and that's what
而且我可能没空理你，因为我要全程跳舞，那才是我

1570
01:07:47.070 --> 01:07:48.070
I want for my party.
想要的派对。

1571
01:07:48.510 --> 01:07:53.010
But for my 40th, I was seven months pregnant with my daughter.
但我四十岁生日时，怀我女儿已经七个月了。

1572
01:07:53.490 --> 01:07:57.290
And so Lee and I just went and had a little baby moon slash birthday.
所以李和我只是去度了个小小的产前蜜月兼生日旅行。

1573
01:07:57.810 --> 01:08:01.450
So it'll be like 20 years since I had a dance party.
算下来我都有二十年没办过舞会了。

1574
01:08:01.450 --> 01:08:08.010
Well, I can't wait because I want me, you, and Oscar to recreate what we did for years,
我等不及了，因为我想让你、我和奥斯卡重现我们当年的经典表演，

1575
01:08:08.010 --> 01:08:11.490
which was we did All the Single Ladies by Beyonce.
就是碧昂丝的《单身女郎》。

1576
01:08:11.910 --> 01:08:12.630
The three of us.
我们三个一起。

1577
01:08:12.730 --> 01:08:13.930
I want all the single ladies.
我要跳《单身女郎》。

1578
01:08:13.950 --> 01:08:15.310
I want sexy back.
我要跳《SexyBack》。

1579
01:08:15.650 --> 01:08:16.710
I want gold digger.
我要跳《Gold Digger》。

1580
01:08:16.870 --> 01:08:18.070
I want some Lady Gaga.
我还要跳Lady Gaga的歌。

1581
01:08:18.430 --> 01:08:18.930
Oh, yeah.
噢，太棒了。

1582
01:08:19.070 --> 01:08:19.870
I want them all.
我全都要跳。

1583
01:08:20.350 --> 01:08:26.210
I just rewatched my wedding video because for my anniversary this year, my husband finally
我刚重温了我的婚礼录像，因为今年结婚纪念日，我丈夫终于

1584
01:08:26.210 --> 01:08:28.450
edited together all the footage from our wedding.
把我们婚礼的所有素材剪辑到了一起。

1585
01:08:28.690 --> 01:08:28.950
Really?
真的吗？

1586
01:08:29.270 --> 01:08:29.630
Yes.
是的。

1587
01:08:29.630 --> 01:08:34.310
He said it took him a year because he just had to work on it a little bit at a time.
他说他花了一年时间，因为他只能一点一点地剪。

1588
01:08:35.130 --> 01:08:38.510
It's almost 30 minutes, and we sat down with the kids and watched it.
视频有快三十分钟长，我们和孩子们坐在一起看了。

1589
01:08:38.870 --> 01:08:42.330
And it was so fun to see all of us dancing, Jenna.
看到我们大家都在跳舞真是太有趣了，珍娜。

1590
01:08:42.590 --> 01:08:46.070
I mean, there were so many elements that were great, but it just warmed my heart.
我是说，有很多精彩的片段，但那一幕真的暖到了我。

1591
01:08:46.250 --> 01:08:47.610
Like, there you are on the dance floor.
就像，你就在舞池里。

1592
01:08:47.770 --> 01:08:49.390
We're, like, dancing our hearts out.
我们都在尽情地跳舞。

1593
01:08:49.830 --> 01:08:50.870
It's just so great.
那感觉太棒了。

1594
01:08:51.330 --> 01:08:52.350
Well, I want it.
总之，我想要那样的派对。

1595
01:08:53.070 --> 01:08:53.910
You're going to have it.
你会有的。

1596
01:08:53.970 --> 01:08:55.010
You're going to have a dance party.
你会拥有一场舞会的。

1597
01:08:55.210 --> 01:08:55.810
Okay, good.
好的，太好了。

1598
01:08:55.810 --> 01:09:00.670
We painted hummingbirds for my 50th, and by God, we're going to dance on your 50th.
我五十岁时画了蜂鸟，老天作证，你五十岁时我们一定要跳舞。

1599
01:09:00.950 --> 01:09:01.350
Good.
好。

1600
01:09:01.910 --> 01:09:02.470
Yay.
耶。

1601
01:09:02.830 --> 01:09:04.270
I'm going to make sure it happens.
我会确保这件事发生。

1602
01:09:04.990 --> 01:09:09.930
Well, there's one person who refuses to dance in cafe disco, and that is Angela.
嗯，有一个人拒绝在咖啡厅迪斯科跳舞，那就是安吉拉。

1603
01:09:09.930 --> 01:09:16.470
But, but, she's going to sway her foot a little bit to the music.
但是，但是，她会随着音乐稍微晃动一下脚。

1604
01:09:16.670 --> 01:09:17.830
She's going to tap her finger.
她会用手指打拍子。

1605
01:09:18.130 --> 01:09:18.330
Yeah.
没错。

1606
01:09:18.830 --> 01:09:27.490
And Halstead shared that this whole storyline of Michael starting a cafe disco was always going to end with this moment.
哈尔斯特德分享说，迈克尔开办咖啡厅迪斯科的整个故事线，注定要以这一刻作为结局。

1607
01:09:27.970 --> 01:09:29.390
I did not know that.
我之前不知道这一点。

1608
01:09:29.610 --> 01:09:37.730
He said that their litmus test for whether or not Michael could pull off his cafe disco dream was Angela,
他说，他们衡量迈克尔能否实现咖啡厅迪斯科梦想的试金石就是安吉拉，

1609
01:09:37.730 --> 01:09:41.430
because she thought that hanging out at a disco all day was completely unacceptable.
因为她认为整天泡在迪斯科舞厅里是完全不可接受的。

1610
01:09:41.590 --> 01:09:49.030
She was the lone holdout through most of the show, and Michael, if you notice, keeps checking in with her, checking in with her, trying to engage her.
在节目的大部分时间里，她是唯一的反对者，而且如果你注意观察，迈克尔一直在关注她，不断确认她的反应，试图让她参与进来。

1611
01:09:49.030 --> 01:09:55.890
So, in the end, that little tap and that little foot sway, that is Michael's victory.
所以，最后那轻轻的一点拍子和脚部晃动，就是迈克尔的胜利。

1612
01:09:56.050 --> 01:09:56.990
That's his big win.
那是他的一大成就。

1613
01:09:57.350 --> 01:10:06.350
And Warren shared, by the way, that in his mind, he thought that this moment actually is the beginning of an evolution for the character of Angela.
顺便说一下，沃伦分享说，在他看来，他认为这一刻实际上是安吉拉这个角色进化的开始。

1614
01:10:06.810 --> 01:10:16.530
That this moment that shows how severe and closed off her character can be, but it's a baby step toward her maybe opening up to new possibilities.
这一刻展示了她的性格可以多么严肃和封闭，但这也是她迈向可能拥抱新可能的一小步。

1615
01:10:16.970 --> 01:10:17.890
Ooh, I like that.
噢，我喜欢这个解读。

1616
01:10:17.890 --> 01:10:23.130
So, this moment was very rich in their outline and their writing of this episode.
所以，在这一集的提纲和剧本创作中，这一刻是非常丰富的。

1617
01:10:23.270 --> 01:10:24.690
And very thought out.
而且经过了深思熟虑。

1618
01:10:24.950 --> 01:10:25.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1619
01:10:25.810 --> 01:10:28.050
Well, I went to the script.
我查阅了剧本。

1620
01:10:28.270 --> 01:10:30.990
I wanted to see what was in the shooting draft for this moment.
我想看看拍摄初稿中关于这一刻的内容。

1621
01:10:31.450 --> 01:10:33.190
There was a Michael voiceover.
当时有一段迈克尔的旁白。

1622
01:10:33.550 --> 01:10:34.950
Here's what it says in the script.
剧本里是这样写的。

1623
01:10:35.290 --> 01:10:36.630
Michael sits with Angela.
迈克尔和安吉拉坐在一起。

1624
01:10:36.990 --> 01:10:47.690
He looks around the room and takes in all of the dancing couples, Jim and Pam, Phyllis and Bob, Kelly and Andy, and Kevin and Lynn, who are furiously making out.
他环顾四周，看着所有跳舞的情侣：吉姆和帕姆、菲利斯和鲍勃、凯利和安迪，还有正在疯狂亲热的凯文和琳恩。

1625
01:10:47.890 --> 01:10:52.670
Michael notices Angela is tapping her foot to the music and he smiles to himself.
迈克尔注意到安吉拉正随着音乐打拍子，他会心地笑了。

1626
01:10:52.990 --> 01:10:55.370
And this is the voiceover that would then play.
这就是随后会播放的旁白。

1627
01:10:55.810 --> 01:10:56.870
They needed me.
他们需要我。

1628
01:10:57.190 --> 01:10:58.070
I left.
我离开了。

1629
01:10:58.270 --> 01:11:00.330
I will never let them down again.
我再也不会让他们失望了。

1630
01:11:00.610 --> 01:11:02.390
I will always be there for them.
我会永远支持他们。

1631
01:11:02.390 --> 01:11:13.130
I will be at every important moment of their lives, their births, their deaths, their babies, other hospital stuff, no matter where or whether they want me there or not.
我会出现在他们生命中的每一个重要时刻，他们的出生、死亡、生孩子，以及其他医院里的事，无论在哪里，也无论他们是否希望我在场。

1632
01:11:13.590 --> 01:11:14.470
For them.
为了他们。

1633
01:11:15.410 --> 01:11:17.810
That actually made me get a little choked up.
那段话真的让我有点哽咽。

1634
01:11:18.170 --> 01:11:18.870
I know.
我知道。

1635
01:11:19.010 --> 01:11:19.950
Isn't that so sweet?
是不是很贴心？

1636
01:11:19.950 --> 01:11:21.550
I really wish that had been in.
我真希望那段话能保留下来。

1637
01:11:21.770 --> 01:11:22.330
I know.
我知道。

1638
01:11:22.330 --> 01:11:23.770
I thought that was really sweet.
我觉得那真的很感人。

1639
01:11:24.290 --> 01:11:34.710
One other thing I want to share is that when we were filming in Cafe Disco and trying to figure out this moment of how Michael would see my foot swaying, my finger tapping,
我还想分享另一件事，当我们拍摄咖啡厅迪斯科，试图构思迈克尔如何看到我晃动脚、手指打拍子这一刻时，

1640
01:11:35.070 --> 01:11:39.570
we shot just a quick little tag that didn't make it in.
我们拍了一个没用上的小尾声。

1641
01:11:39.570 --> 01:11:44.950
And everyone has left Cafe Disco and only Angela Martin is in there cleaning.
当时所有人都离开了咖啡厅迪斯科，只有安吉拉·马丁在里面打扫卫生。

1642
01:11:46.230 --> 01:11:50.350
And Michael walks by and she is dancing as she cleans.
迈克尔走过时，她正一边打扫一边跳舞。

1643
01:11:50.730 --> 01:11:52.750
Why do I remember this?
为什么我记得这个？

1644
01:11:53.030 --> 01:11:57.290
We just shot it really quickly and just as an alt, just in case.
我们只是很快地拍了一下，作为一个备选方案，以防万一。

1645
01:11:57.290 --> 01:11:57.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1646
01:11:58.130 --> 01:12:02.230
Like you actually respond to the music when everybody's left.
就像当所有人都离开后，你真的对音乐有了反应。

1647
01:12:02.570 --> 01:12:03.090
Everyone's left.
所有人都离开了。

1648
01:12:03.090 --> 01:12:03.890
But it's still that victory.
但这依然是一种胜利。

1649
01:12:04.030 --> 01:12:04.910
He still got you.
他最终还是赢得了你。

1650
01:12:05.030 --> 01:12:05.250
Yeah.
没错。

1651
01:12:05.370 --> 01:12:06.730
But that didn't make it in.
但那段没用上。

1652
01:12:06.830 --> 01:12:07.770
It's not in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里没有。

1653
01:12:07.870 --> 01:12:08.970
It's not in deleted scenes.
删减片段里也没有。

1654
01:12:09.250 --> 01:12:11.670
But that was an alt that they shot.
但那是他们拍的一个备选方案。

1655
01:12:11.990 --> 01:12:16.750
I wonder if we were all like waiting in the hallway while you did that or something because I have such a memory of it.
我在想当时我们是不是都在走廊里等着，因为我对那件事印象特别深。

1656
01:12:16.890 --> 01:12:17.690
It was really quick.
当时拍得很快。

1657
01:12:17.690 --> 01:12:19.370
We just sort of grabbed it in the moment.
我们就是临时起意拍的。

1658
01:12:19.670 --> 01:12:26.990
But of course, the actual tag that made it in, which is so great, is Kelly piercing Andy's ear in the restroom.
不过当然，最终用上的那个片尾彩蛋非常棒，就是凯莉在洗手间给安迪穿耳洞。

1659
01:12:27.290 --> 01:12:31.110
This really lends itself to that idea that they could be a couple.
这确实让人觉得他们俩很像是一对。

1660
01:12:31.390 --> 01:12:32.010
I know.
我知道。

1661
01:12:32.490 --> 01:12:34.010
Because this is a very cute couple-y thing.
因为这确实是很可爱的情侣行为。

1662
01:12:34.150 --> 01:12:34.770
It is.
确实是。

1663
01:12:34.870 --> 01:12:41.690
And Halstead said that they actually did a take where Mindy, as Kelly, fully pierces Andy's ear.
哈尔斯特德说他们其实拍过一个版本，明迪饰演的凯莉真的把安迪的耳朵穿透了。

1664
01:12:41.850 --> 01:12:43.290
And it was painful and bloody.
当时又疼又流血。

1665
01:12:43.570 --> 01:12:44.210
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1666
01:12:44.210 --> 01:12:44.910
And a mess.
而且一团糟。

1667
01:12:45.070 --> 01:12:46.450
But they cut it for time.
但为了控制时长被剪掉了。

1668
01:12:48.530 --> 01:12:49.910
Well, that's it, guys.
好了，就是这样，伙计们。

1669
01:12:49.930 --> 01:12:51.230
That's Cafe Disco.
这就是《咖啡迪斯科》。

1670
01:12:51.490 --> 01:12:52.190
It is.
没错。

1671
01:12:52.190 --> 01:12:53.530
And it was so fun.
真的太有趣了。

1672
01:12:53.530 --> 01:12:54.950
I loved re-watching this.
重温这一集我非常喜欢。

1673
01:12:54.950 --> 01:13:01.650
Thank you so much to Warren Lieberstein and Halstead Sullivan, Randy Cordray, for giving us all kinds of fun behind-the-scenes details.
非常感谢沃伦·利伯斯坦、哈尔斯特德·沙利文和兰迪·科德雷，为我们提供了各种有趣的幕后细节。

1674
01:13:01.950 --> 01:13:06.530
And, lady, before we go, you know how at the beginning of the episodes we always say, like, when do you listen?
还有，女士，在结束之前，你知道我们在每集开头总是会问，大家都在什么时候听吗？

1675
01:13:06.530 --> 01:13:07.450
Where do you listen?
大家都在哪里听？

1676
01:13:07.490 --> 01:13:08.870
You always say good morning.
你总是说早上好。

1677
01:13:09.090 --> 01:13:09.210
Yes.
是的。

1678
01:13:09.210 --> 01:13:11.570
And then you remember that people might not listen in the morning.
然后你就会想起大家可能不是在早上听的。

1679
01:13:11.830 --> 01:13:12.090
Yes.
没错。

1680
01:13:12.370 --> 01:13:17.850
Well, we got a letter from Katie C., who is 14 years old, lives in the UK.
我们收到了一封来自凯蒂·C的信，她14岁，住在英国。

1681
01:13:18.070 --> 01:13:19.250
And she said,
她说，

1682
01:13:19.390 --> 01:13:26.090
I listen to Office Ladies whilst delivering newspapers every day, and it makes it so much more fun.
我每天送报纸的时候都会听《办公室女士》，这让送报变得有趣多了。

1683
01:13:26.190 --> 01:13:34.070
When it's raining or way too warm, for my ginger jeans, I know I have the podcast to keep me going, and I never give up.
每当下雨或者天气太热，让我这双姜黄色的牛仔裤难受时，我知道有播客陪着我，我就永远不会放弃。

1684
01:13:34.070 --> 01:13:35.930
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1685
01:13:36.270 --> 01:13:37.010
Well, hi, Katie.
你好啊，凯蒂。

1686
01:13:37.310 --> 01:13:38.130
Hi, Katie.
你好，凯蒂。

1687
01:13:38.430 --> 01:13:40.170
Good luck today on your paper route.
祝你今天的送报工作顺利。

1688
01:13:40.330 --> 01:13:40.930
Be safe.
注意安全。

1689
01:13:41.110 --> 01:13:43.070
And Jenna and I are sending you big hugs.
我和珍娜给你一个大大的拥抱。

1690
01:13:43.250 --> 01:13:44.810
Thanks for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1691
01:13:49.230 --> 01:13:51.270
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

